WEBVTT

00:45.128 --> 00:48.715
I studied Geophysics, but I dropped out.

00:48.798 --> 00:50.383
Once I finished service,

00:50.884 --> 00:53.470
I took the Civil Service Exam
and went to the KMA.

00:54.137 --> 00:56.014
I'm Level Seven, Severe Weather.

00:58.850 --> 00:59.768
Hmm.

01:01.936 --> 01:05.315
Your parents, are they still working?

01:09.152 --> 01:15.867
We did a CT scan and there's a mass
of about 3 centimeters on his right lung.

01:15.950 --> 01:17.368
We should investigate.

01:17.452 --> 01:20.288
Going forward,
I'd highly recommend a biopsy.

01:26.127 --> 01:29.047
My mother isn't with us.
She died years ago.

01:31.382 --> 01:32.467
My dad…

01:37.597 --> 01:41.184
…was a construction worker
till he got hurt.

01:42.519 --> 01:44.145
He can't work 'cause of that.

01:50.860 --> 01:52.070
Oh, oh…

01:54.280 --> 01:55.532
I see.

02:05.834 --> 02:07.669
The rain said to the wind…

02:08.628 --> 02:11.089
BIOPSY CONSENT FORM

02:11.172 --> 02:13.383
He'll need to stay
at the hospital for a day,

02:13.466 --> 02:15.135
maybe two for the biopsy.

02:15.718 --> 02:18.263
Also, we need
a guardian signature right there.

02:20.723 --> 02:22.725
PATIENT OR GUARDIAN SIGNATURE

02:34.863 --> 02:37.824
…"You roar. And I'll fall."

02:49.127 --> 02:54.757
EPISODE 15
ENSEMBLE

02:58.678 --> 02:59.888
Where are you going?

02:59.971 --> 03:00.972
Oh…

03:02.265 --> 03:03.892
Oh, you're still here?

03:05.810 --> 03:08.396
You're not supposed
to be walking around. Don't leave.

03:08.479 --> 03:12.358
Ah, these insurance assholes
are so intense now.

03:12.442 --> 03:15.028
They're acting
like I'm some insurance scam

03:15.111 --> 03:17.071
wherein they said the cops are watching.

03:17.155 --> 03:18.406
They don't believe you?

03:19.073 --> 03:21.534
Seriously, I was just crossing the road,

03:21.618 --> 03:24.329
and then this car
was going so fast that it hit me.

03:28.041 --> 03:28.875
Wait a sec.

03:30.376 --> 03:32.545
Si-woo didn't come with you, huh?

03:32.629 --> 03:35.381
There wasn't any time for me
to call him. I'll call him now.

03:35.465 --> 03:38.259
Nah. Bothering him is not worth it.

03:38.343 --> 03:41.721
Swear I'll send you the money
for the hospital bill and all that.

03:42.305 --> 03:45.892
So you don't have
to nag Si-woo about it. Deal?

03:48.102 --> 03:51.231
The doctor said
they need to do more tests.

03:53.524 --> 03:55.193
You're more gullible than I thought.

03:56.110 --> 03:59.322
A hospital is just trying to get
as much out of you as they can.

03:59.405 --> 04:00.406
You know what I'm saying?

04:00.990 --> 04:03.326
It's on the CAT scan.
Something's on your lung.

04:03.409 --> 04:05.119
That happens to everyone.

04:05.203 --> 04:08.623
When you get old, you get lumps
and stuff. It's natural.

04:13.253 --> 04:14.712
Were you already aware of it?

04:17.882 --> 04:22.637
Hey, lady, if you got any money,
you know, 10 thou,

04:22.720 --> 04:25.348
would you spot me, so I can get a bite?

04:30.395 --> 04:31.729
They wanna do a biopsy.

04:31.813 --> 04:34.691
I gave them your information.
You'd stay here a day or two.

04:37.318 --> 04:38.945
I strongly recommend doing it.

04:39.696 --> 04:41.155
But it's really up to you.

04:41.781 --> 04:43.533
Si-woo doesn't need to know, okay?

04:46.244 --> 04:47.829
It's our secret.

04:55.503 --> 04:56.879
Turn it off.

04:57.505 --> 04:59.424
Oh, I'm sorry.

05:24.574 --> 05:25.783
Eomma, you're here.

05:29.704 --> 05:31.247
I had some thinking to do.

05:31.998 --> 05:33.666
Why? You can't think at your own house?

05:34.917 --> 05:36.252
I guess not.

05:36.836 --> 05:40.840
Oh, I saw Lee Si-woo
and we had a little talk.

05:42.550 --> 05:44.010
Mom, why was Lee Si-woo here?

05:44.510 --> 05:45.720
What do you mean "little talk"?

05:47.805 --> 05:49.182
Why is it so important, huh?

05:49.265 --> 05:51.017
If you're not dating anymore.

05:52.769 --> 05:53.978
We aren't, but…

05:55.855 --> 05:57.273
It's good that you did.

05:57.357 --> 05:59.776
There's no need for every boyfriend
to be a husband.

06:00.443 --> 06:01.736
You should get some rest.

06:35.561 --> 06:37.855
Door is opening.

06:45.947 --> 06:47.365
Door is closing.

07:38.499 --> 07:40.543
The first cold wave
of the season is persisting,

07:40.626 --> 07:43.671
and Seoul saw its first frost of the year.

07:43.754 --> 07:47.758
The temperature is continuing to drop,
while Seoul is currently three degrees.

07:47.842 --> 07:51.179
The low today is 0.7 degrees in the city.

07:51.262 --> 07:54.807
The KMA forecast predicts
chilly temperatures this evening

07:54.891 --> 07:57.393
with things warming up closer
to average temperatures

07:57.477 --> 07:59.395
for the season by tomorrow afternoon.

07:59.479 --> 08:02.815
However, the midlands
will be trading the cold weather

08:02.899 --> 08:04.525
for strong winds.

08:04.609 --> 08:07.653
We recommend taking precautions
against those high winds.

08:07.737 --> 08:10.907
The air today is fairly clear.
The daily average for the fine dust level

08:10.990 --> 08:13.951
is in the good to normal range
for the entire country.

08:14.035 --> 08:17.121
Far from shore, and the skies
to the central Southeast--

08:21.000 --> 08:24.420
You don't have to come in.
I can see the doctor alone.

08:28.841 --> 08:30.384
Why aren't you saying anything?

08:31.594 --> 08:33.346
I'm thinking about what you said.

08:35.097 --> 08:37.058
Can I have a little while
to think about it?

08:38.226 --> 08:41.604
If we wait too long,
then they can't do anything for me.

08:47.818 --> 08:50.613
Every time I try to think it through,
we just can't afford it.

08:52.323 --> 08:54.116
Having a kid is costly.

08:54.742 --> 08:57.245
The doctor visits, delivery, the recovery.

08:57.328 --> 08:59.121
We can move somewhere cheaper,

09:00.122 --> 09:02.375
then we could scrape together enough
for the birth cost.

09:02.458 --> 09:04.001
After that, I don't know.

09:09.549 --> 09:11.634
It doesn't get cheaper
once the baby's here.

09:12.218 --> 09:15.638
I'd use up my maternity leave
and we'd need to get a nanny.

09:15.721 --> 09:19.767
I looked into it, and they cost
as much as my starting salary.

09:23.020 --> 09:26.524
There's kindergarten
or there's something like that.

09:27.525 --> 09:30.278
There's a while
when the kid's too young for daycare.

09:34.490 --> 09:36.492
Oppa, you go to work
when the sun comes up.

09:36.576 --> 09:38.077
And I stay late almost every day.

09:38.661 --> 09:41.956
There's parental leave.
And you could take extra time off.

09:44.709 --> 09:45.960
I couldn't go back.

09:46.043 --> 09:49.046
I just got my own column.
They're giving me a chance.

09:49.130 --> 09:51.090
I don't want to give up this opportunity.

09:51.173 --> 09:52.967
And I don't want to give up
my career either.

10:00.141 --> 10:02.518
We got married really impulsively.

10:03.728 --> 10:06.689
And we really can't bring a child
into the world like that.

10:30.755 --> 10:32.381
Hello? What do you need?

10:32.465 --> 10:34.091
Hey.

10:34.175 --> 10:36.594
They say they might do it this afternoon.

10:36.677 --> 10:39.555
They're doing a blood test
and some other things.

10:41.599 --> 10:42.642
Oh, all right.

10:43.309 --> 10:44.977
They said I can't eat after ten.

10:45.811 --> 10:47.813
I should have had more food.

10:47.897 --> 10:50.066
I had breakfast,
but I would have eaten more.

10:50.149 --> 10:52.026
Jeez, I'm hungry.

10:52.109 --> 10:55.196
I'm heading into work right now,
and I'll be in a meeting right after.

10:55.988 --> 10:57.073
Oh, hey.

10:58.240 --> 11:01.285
Si-woo doesn't… know yet, does he?

11:02.495 --> 11:03.829
I have to go. Goodbye.

11:14.632 --> 11:17.677
Huh? Why are you here?

11:17.760 --> 11:19.470
- You slept here?
- Oh!

11:19.553 --> 11:22.056
Uh, no, it's not that. No.

11:22.139 --> 11:23.808
Your apartment search failed?

11:26.185 --> 11:28.354
Don't tell, um, the Director, please.

11:28.437 --> 11:30.856
Why? You two had a fight?

11:30.940 --> 11:33.567
No. I don't want her to worry.

11:34.402 --> 11:35.611
You're too sweet, you know.

11:35.695 --> 11:37.822
Go on, get.

11:45.079 --> 11:47.248
- Good morning, everyone.
- Hmm.

11:47.331 --> 11:49.625
- Working hard?
- You're here early.

11:49.709 --> 11:52.920
Ooh, today looks like
it's a lot colder than we forecast.

11:53.003 --> 11:54.088
Nah, it'll be fine.

11:54.171 --> 11:58.092
The continental anticyclone
in Siberia has momentarily strengthened.

11:58.175 --> 12:00.052
But there's a strong warm current
in the south,

12:00.136 --> 12:01.512
so tomorrow, it will be warm again.

12:01.595 --> 12:03.597
And our ensemble forecast then?

12:03.681 --> 12:06.475
Ms. Lee, would you give me
the ensemble we printed earlier?

12:06.559 --> 12:08.644
ENSEMBLE FORECASTING: A METHOD
THAT MINIMIZES ERRORS AND UNCERTAINTIES

12:08.728 --> 12:10.354
BY USING SEVERAL NUMERICAL MODELS
TO MAKE VARIOUS PREDICTIONS

12:10.438 --> 12:12.106
- Here.
- Here you are.

12:12.940 --> 12:16.360
The NWP model and the ensemble prediction

12:16.444 --> 12:18.946
all show temperatures
rising tomorrow afternoon.

12:19.029 --> 12:20.030
So I see.

12:20.114 --> 12:23.325
We shouldn't have to change that much
from what we sent out yesterday.

12:24.326 --> 12:26.912
Well, looks like an easy one,
all thanks to you.

12:26.996 --> 12:28.581
You got a great Team One, Director.

12:35.671 --> 12:36.964
Good morning.

12:37.047 --> 12:38.382
- Hello.
- Hi.

12:38.466 --> 12:39.967
Good morning. Oh, right.

12:41.427 --> 12:43.179
You left this at my apartment yesterday.

12:43.888 --> 12:44.972
Ah…

12:46.515 --> 12:47.683
Right.

12:48.559 --> 12:50.352
I guess I was sort of scattered.

12:50.436 --> 12:53.105
My mother often does that
to people that she sees.

12:55.649 --> 12:57.109
Oh, that's very nice.

13:04.116 --> 13:05.409
Let's talk later.

13:07.745 --> 13:09.079
Oh, yeah.

13:15.920 --> 13:17.880
He's already meeting her mom?

13:18.547 --> 13:20.883
Oh, wow.
It's going really well.

13:22.009 --> 13:23.385
Don't get ahead of yourselves.

13:23.469 --> 13:25.888
Stop being so sour.
They're great.

13:36.565 --> 13:37.691
Yes?

13:37.775 --> 13:39.109
I'm not supposed to…

13:39.777 --> 13:41.862
have water on my fast, right?

13:41.946 --> 13:44.657
I'm at work and I can't talk.
I'm so sorry.

14:08.889 --> 14:09.932
You want a coffee?

14:13.060 --> 14:14.144
Oh, sure.

14:33.163 --> 14:34.373
Hey, uh…

14:34.999 --> 14:37.918
Have you called and talked
to your father recently?

14:40.379 --> 14:41.213
Why?

14:43.507 --> 14:46.886
It's just it's starting
to get a bit colder, so I…

14:46.969 --> 14:49.096
I told you. We don't chitchat like that.

14:53.559 --> 14:56.437
It's not too hard just to call
and check on him, though, right?

14:56.520 --> 14:57.980
It's not that it's hard.

14:58.480 --> 14:59.773
I don't want to.

15:02.693 --> 15:05.738
Still, your father's getting older.
It wouldn't be the worst for you to try.

15:06.989 --> 15:09.241
Not all dads in this world
are someone you talk to.

15:09.325 --> 15:11.493
In his whole life, he's never cared

15:11.577 --> 15:14.371
how I was doing
or whether I was feeling all right.

15:14.455 --> 15:16.582
And I don't see why
I shouldn't act like that too.

15:16.665 --> 15:18.709
You think we should call just to talk?

15:18.792 --> 15:20.544
I don't think he wants us to.

15:20.628 --> 15:22.546
Regardless of how the weather goes.

15:26.967 --> 15:28.469
You'll regret this.

15:30.846 --> 15:33.807
If you ignore him now
out of some sort of anger,

15:34.683 --> 15:38.020
you could regret it down the road, still.

15:41.899 --> 15:45.361
And you can never go back
no matter how much it hurts.

15:45.444 --> 15:46.278
I won't.

15:47.154 --> 15:49.114
I won't ever regret it. I swear.

15:50.157 --> 15:53.452
There's no moment
I want to redo, not with…

15:54.870 --> 15:56.205
Not with him.

16:10.970 --> 16:14.056
We had a disagreement over his father.

16:15.599 --> 16:17.059
I don't need to know that.

16:19.395 --> 16:21.105
No, you don't.

16:23.607 --> 16:26.360
PART-TIME HOUSEKEEPER

16:28.904 --> 16:31.532
LOOKING FOR A PART-TIME HOUSEKEEPER

16:31.615 --> 16:33.200
HIRING FULL-TIME HOUSEKEEPERS

16:36.286 --> 16:40.290
DIAPER COSTS PER MONTH

16:48.674 --> 16:51.343
BABY FORMULA COST PER MONTH

17:16.702 --> 17:18.454
- Sir.
- Yeah?

17:19.830 --> 17:21.331
Aren't you gonna eat?

17:21.915 --> 17:25.377
Oh. I'm not… really hungry.

17:25.461 --> 17:27.337
- You please go on.
- Okay, well, um…

17:27.421 --> 17:28.547
Yeah.

17:29.381 --> 17:32.009
Sir, are you gonna eat?

17:32.843 --> 17:34.511
Oh, it's time already?

17:35.179 --> 17:37.890
Really? Okay. Let's eat. Let's eat.

17:38.474 --> 17:41.435
- Come on. Let's all go, huh? Let's all go.
- I'll go, then.

17:41.518 --> 17:44.897
I… I'm really not hungry.
Seriously. You can go.

17:44.980 --> 17:46.398
- Suit yourself.
- Yeah.

17:46.482 --> 17:47.524
Let's go eat.

17:48.484 --> 17:50.027
What should we get today?

17:51.653 --> 17:53.197
Ah, let's go.

18:02.372 --> 18:04.208
PARENTING COMMUNITY

18:08.253 --> 18:09.713
JOIN COMMUNITY

18:09.797 --> 18:11.590
SUBMIT INFORMATION TO JOIN COMMUNITY

18:11.673 --> 18:14.927
BABY BUMP NICKNAME

18:24.103 --> 18:25.187
Yeah, yeah.

18:25.270 --> 18:28.398
So, uh, you talked to Bo-mi yet?

18:28.482 --> 18:30.734
Yes. However, um…

18:30.818 --> 18:32.152
What does she want?

18:32.236 --> 18:34.404
- She wants to go eat.
- Wait, huh?

18:34.947 --> 18:37.032
Not some new clothes or some sort of--

18:37.116 --> 18:39.535
No. I was told she doesn't want clothes.

18:39.618 --> 18:41.745
She wants a meal with her eomma and appa.

18:41.829 --> 18:43.872
I can't remember the last time

18:43.956 --> 18:46.041
the three of us
went out to eat altogether.

18:46.125 --> 18:47.292
I'm sure she can't either.

18:47.876 --> 18:50.379
When was it?
When she was five or six?

18:50.462 --> 18:51.797
Uh…

18:51.880 --> 18:55.425
I know we went
to that family restaurant then.

18:55.509 --> 18:58.095
Of course, we had
that big argument on the way home.

18:58.762 --> 19:01.473
Oh, right. Right. Mm.

19:01.557 --> 19:05.102
Okay. I'll call her tutor
and cancel her private session today,

19:05.185 --> 19:06.395
so get a reservation.

19:06.478 --> 19:07.938
Mm-hmm. Mm-hmm.

19:08.021 --> 19:10.315
Tell me where,
and I'll take Bo-mi there, okay?

19:10.899 --> 19:12.568
Also, Bo-mi likes pasta.

19:12.651 --> 19:13.694
Pasta.

19:14.194 --> 19:15.612
Yeah. Thank you.

19:20.492 --> 19:24.705
Um Dong-han. What were you thinking?

19:24.788 --> 19:28.458
Even way back then, you were always…

19:29.293 --> 19:30.794
- an ass.
- Mr. Um.

19:30.878 --> 19:33.505
I printed out the data on the ECMWF.

19:33.589 --> 19:35.257
It's on your desk to review.

19:35.340 --> 19:36.675
I'll also have the KIM for you.

19:36.758 --> 19:38.385
Okay, all right.

19:46.977 --> 19:49.313
- Here's the citrus tea you ordered.
- Oh, thanks so much.

19:49.396 --> 19:50.939
A citrus tea also. Thank you.

19:51.523 --> 19:53.525
Oh, Mr. Kim.

19:54.151 --> 19:55.652
Ah, hmm, yeah.

19:55.736 --> 19:57.237
It's cold, huh?

19:57.321 --> 20:00.282
It got so cold around here. It happened
in such a short time, you know.

20:00.365 --> 20:03.118
Yeah. There's no middle ground
in this country.

20:03.202 --> 20:04.369
Right.

20:04.453 --> 20:07.372
Oh, how is your…
your new recruit coming along?

20:07.956 --> 20:08.999
Hmm?

20:11.668 --> 20:14.171
I don't know what to say to you
to make you understand,

20:14.254 --> 20:17.507
but it's necessary to always do this
with the high-res reports.

20:18.091 --> 20:20.928
You told me to look
at the forecast field report, sir,

20:21.011 --> 20:21.970
not those.

20:26.642 --> 20:29.478
You've been here long enough.
You should know how to perform your role.

20:31.063 --> 20:33.315
- I'm sorry.
- Redo it all.

20:34.441 --> 20:35.567
Okay.

20:40.280 --> 20:43.033
What? What is it? Do you want some help?

20:43.116 --> 20:44.910
Oh, no.

20:52.292 --> 20:55.629
I heard that the Policy Division's
been searching for a way to poach her.

20:57.130 --> 20:58.090
You didn't know?

21:03.136 --> 21:06.098
It's hard, right?
Here, drink that. Citrus tea.

21:06.682 --> 21:08.558
Oh, thank you.

21:31.540 --> 21:32.499
Director.

21:33.000 --> 21:36.336
The air pressure flow
looks kinda odd, huh?

21:36.420 --> 21:37.379
Where?

21:37.462 --> 21:40.424
Here. The way the jet stream
isn't weakening,

21:40.507 --> 21:44.052
I don't think the upper COL
is headed eastwards at all now.

21:48.390 --> 21:52.561
The NWP model has the temperature
going back up tomorrow afternoon.

21:52.644 --> 21:55.314
Yeah, that's that, but Si-woo, come here.

21:55.397 --> 21:56.231
Okay.

22:02.029 --> 22:03.905
Here. What do you think of this?

22:05.407 --> 22:06.450
Hmm.

22:08.577 --> 22:10.829
I think we should compare it
to the real condition data

22:10.912 --> 22:13.290
and analyze the possible outcomes
for this pattern.

22:13.373 --> 22:14.624
Yeah. Something's not right.

22:14.708 --> 22:16.626
- Yeah.
- What is it? I…

22:16.710 --> 22:19.629
If you look here, the jet stream's
expansion is too stable.

22:19.713 --> 22:22.090
There's not really a record
of this sort of behavior, right?

22:22.174 --> 22:24.176
Yeah. That's what I find strange too.

22:28.013 --> 22:30.182
Let's look
at the ensemble prediction,

22:30.265 --> 22:32.517
and perform an analysis on the scenarios

22:32.601 --> 22:35.270
that suggest a cold wave
could carry on for a while.

22:35.354 --> 22:37.230
Okay. On our meeting, I'm gonna

22:37.314 --> 22:39.691
go of the current NWP,
if that's all right.

22:39.775 --> 22:40.650
Mm-hmm.

22:41.610 --> 22:44.946
Mr. Shin. Send me time series data
for the major regions.

22:45.030 --> 22:46.031
Okay.

22:51.244 --> 22:53.288
- Okay, I sent it.
- Mm, okay.

23:12.766 --> 23:14.184
How's work going?

23:15.477 --> 23:18.563
Not great.

23:20.190 --> 23:21.400
How come?

23:30.283 --> 23:32.327
The weather's too nice.

23:37.833 --> 23:40.377
Last time, she said the sky
was too cloudy to work.

23:41.878 --> 23:43.797
She doesn't wanna work
when it's cold either.

23:45.132 --> 23:46.925
Is there anything
I can do to help?

24:03.483 --> 24:04.985
Ma, I'll be out for a little.

24:11.199 --> 24:12.909
Whoa, it's cold.

24:12.993 --> 24:15.871
Eomma, you should have told me
it was so cold.

24:16.788 --> 24:18.373
Where's my fluffy coat?

24:18.457 --> 24:20.208
Mom! My fluffy coat?

24:28.216 --> 24:32.262
I really have to find a coat
at my age for my 40-year-old daughter?

24:32.345 --> 24:33.972
Ma, what's wrong?

24:34.055 --> 24:35.098
You're upset?

24:35.182 --> 24:37.392
I don't even have the energy to be upset.

24:37.476 --> 24:39.603
The both of you are on your own now.

24:39.686 --> 24:41.646
Find the coat and get it yourself.

24:41.730 --> 24:44.941
I don't care.

24:52.365 --> 24:55.160
As predicted,
the cold core is moving south

24:55.243 --> 24:57.496
as the continental anticyclone develops

24:57.579 --> 25:00.499
and national temperatures
are expected to drop 10 to 15 degrees.

25:00.582 --> 25:01.917
Mm, I see.

25:02.000 --> 25:04.461
So then, when do we expect it to end?

25:05.295 --> 25:08.381
According to the NWP
and ensemble prediction modeling,

25:08.465 --> 25:10.217
there's a strong chance
of warmer temperatures

25:10.300 --> 25:11.885
returning tomorrow, however…

25:13.512 --> 25:15.347
Okay, so? However what?

25:17.390 --> 25:20.268
Uh, however,
we're investigating an anomaly

25:20.352 --> 25:21.978
that was found in the ensemble prediction.

25:22.687 --> 25:24.481
And what?

25:25.941 --> 25:27.317
Pull it up.

25:28.902 --> 25:30.070
ENSEMBLE PREDICTION

25:30.153 --> 25:33.240
Of the 32 models
in the ensemble prediction,

25:33.323 --> 25:35.951
there are four showing
three more days of severe cold.

25:36.743 --> 25:38.620
And the whole point
of the ensemble prediction

25:38.703 --> 25:40.372
is to see the outcome
that's more supported.

25:40.455 --> 25:41.706
That's true.

25:41.790 --> 25:43.625
But in this case,
things are a little different.

25:49.256 --> 25:51.841
The biggest thing
is a jet stream 10km high

25:51.925 --> 25:53.885
that isn't losing any strength right now.

25:53.969 --> 25:57.138
And the strong COL at 5km

25:57.222 --> 25:59.266
doesn't look much more likely
to head east.

26:00.684 --> 26:02.727
What? So 4 of 32 models
were like that one?

26:02.811 --> 26:04.896
They're showing a delay
of three to four more days.

26:05.564 --> 26:06.690
Yes.

26:08.149 --> 26:09.192
So now what?

26:09.776 --> 26:10.986
As things are currently--

26:11.069 --> 26:13.863
We may have to retract our forecast.

26:31.923 --> 26:33.258
Forecaster Lee Si-woo.

26:33.842 --> 26:36.177
Do you know what it means for us
to retract a forecast?

26:37.470 --> 26:38.513
Yeah, I'm aware.

26:44.728 --> 26:46.396
And you agree, then?

26:49.065 --> 26:50.317
Retract the forecast?

26:50.400 --> 26:53.236
- No, we can't.
- If we're wrong, it's hell.

27:03.913 --> 27:05.081
Director Jin?

27:06.583 --> 27:07.834
You want to retract it too?

27:09.711 --> 27:10.962
Yes, I'm in favor.

27:30.148 --> 27:32.317
Yes, Mr. Lee. I'm almost at the office.

27:32.400 --> 27:34.361
No! No, no, no, no! Stop, stop!

27:34.444 --> 27:36.905
Turn back around
and go straight to the KMA.

27:36.988 --> 27:40.617
What for? I already sent you
the articles for tomorrow.

27:40.700 --> 27:42.994
The KMA is…

27:44.079 --> 27:45.413
They're retracting their forecast.

27:45.497 --> 27:46.623
What?

27:49.626 --> 27:51.127
What are you going to do?

27:51.670 --> 27:53.171
You'll get backlash if you reverse it,

27:53.254 --> 27:57.384
so you could get the director
of Team One at your throat.

27:57.467 --> 28:00.470
I can't ignore the data
out of fear of others' opinions.

28:00.553 --> 28:03.556
Doesn't the group report show
we could stick with the current forecast?

28:03.640 --> 28:06.393
Well, Mr. Um and Lee Si-woo…

28:07.102 --> 28:08.603
and myself all agree here.

28:09.312 --> 28:12.482
So you're willing to take
all the blame for Lee Si-woo's theory?

28:13.525 --> 28:17.487
You know, I made all these mistakes
when I was younger

28:17.570 --> 28:18.613
and didn't know better.

28:18.697 --> 28:21.366
And my director would cover
for his forecasters.

28:23.243 --> 28:25.453
That's how I got to where I am now.

28:26.037 --> 28:29.082
I'd like to do the same for them now.

28:31.418 --> 28:33.670
Now it's our turn. Now that we're older.

28:39.300 --> 28:42.137
Well, I envy you.

28:43.096 --> 28:47.517
You act, and talk, and behave
like you're really a responsible adult.

28:50.270 --> 28:51.438
Is that sarcasm?

28:52.021 --> 28:54.733
No, seriously. I really mean it.

28:54.816 --> 28:56.359
What's with you all of a sudden?

28:58.111 --> 29:01.531
Recently, I've been feeling like…

29:02.490 --> 29:03.533
You know how they say,

29:03.616 --> 29:06.161
"Nothing's really free in life
and all has a cost"?

29:06.244 --> 29:09.247
And I… have been feeling
so much of that weight,

29:09.330 --> 29:11.207
so much need to be responsible.

29:11.833 --> 29:13.585
And that it's really hard…

29:14.544 --> 29:16.045
to be an adult.

29:21.050 --> 29:25.180
Okay, so if the Chief Team wants
to retract the forecast, we'll retract it.

29:25.263 --> 29:27.432
We'll take care
of whatever comes out of this.

29:30.351 --> 29:32.020
Okay, well, I'll go send it, Director.

29:32.103 --> 29:33.480
Okay.

29:33.563 --> 29:34.647
Yeah, sure.

29:44.365 --> 29:47.160
SI-WOO'S FATHER

29:52.582 --> 29:54.417
Yes, what is it now?

29:55.418 --> 29:57.545
Uh, well, they told me, uh…

29:57.629 --> 30:00.131
They say that I have
to go for my biopsy, so…

30:00.757 --> 30:02.008
Oh, okay.

30:03.092 --> 30:04.344
Well, anyway…

30:06.054 --> 30:08.181
…thank you for the hospital room.

30:08.807 --> 30:11.184
I'm living high,
thanks to my son.

30:11.267 --> 30:15.188
I'll put in a good word for you
with Si-woo sometime.

30:15.814 --> 30:16.648
To be honest,

30:17.148 --> 30:19.609
you're not my type, Director.
You're a little high-strung.

30:20.777 --> 30:24.989
But Si-woo's got a better eye
for, uh, for girls than I do, huh?

30:25.073 --> 30:26.950
Right?

30:27.033 --> 30:28.368
Uh, actually…

30:29.410 --> 30:30.787
we're not together now.

30:33.873 --> 30:34.833
Not together?

30:35.458 --> 30:36.626
Wait, why not?

30:37.710 --> 30:39.212
Hey, did he do something?

30:39.295 --> 30:40.630
Uh, no.

30:40.713 --> 30:41.881
Well, then why?

30:42.841 --> 30:44.509
Wait, did he get aggressive?

30:45.093 --> 30:46.094
No.

30:46.845 --> 30:49.264
That's strange.

30:49.889 --> 30:53.393
He's not the type to stray
or get drunk and make a scene.

30:54.143 --> 30:55.103
Oh, no. Did he?

30:55.979 --> 30:57.230
It wasn't that, sir.

30:57.313 --> 30:58.940
Then why didn't it work?

30:59.816 --> 31:02.277
Why have you been so nice

31:02.360 --> 31:03.278
if you broke up?

31:03.361 --> 31:05.280
Why did you get me that test

31:05.363 --> 31:07.031
and make sure I had a room?

31:07.657 --> 31:11.411
Si-woo's still a part
of our forecasting department here, sir.

31:11.995 --> 31:14.122
As his senior
at work and his director,

31:14.205 --> 31:16.624
it's prudent that I take care
of this for him.

31:19.377 --> 31:22.338
Then I guess you're still hung up
on Si-woo, huh, no?

31:25.133 --> 31:26.593
I gotta take care of something now.

31:26.676 --> 31:28.720
I hope everything goes well
with your biopsy.

31:34.392 --> 31:36.477
What an idiot.

31:37.770 --> 31:39.772
You hold on to a woman like that.

32:08.426 --> 32:09.510
Ms. Chae!

32:10.094 --> 32:12.597
What are you doing here? Are you sick?

32:13.264 --> 32:15.308
It's my stomach.

32:16.559 --> 32:17.518
Are you in pain?

32:18.353 --> 32:19.354
Huh?

32:25.068 --> 32:26.152
You're a little clogged up.

32:27.111 --> 32:29.238
I'm telling you
stress messes with your gut.

32:32.367 --> 32:34.243
Try this. It's herbal medicine.

32:34.327 --> 32:36.162
You wait an hour, you'll feel better.

32:37.872 --> 32:39.582
Don't let yourself suffer.

32:39.666 --> 32:42.001
When life gets hard,
take some medicine, okay?

32:43.252 --> 32:44.295
Mm-hmm.

32:44.379 --> 32:45.505
I'm going in now.

32:46.589 --> 32:47.423
You come in too.

32:57.684 --> 33:00.603
AREUM OBSTETRICS AND GYNECOLOGY
YOUR RESERVATION HAS BEEN CONFIRMED

33:12.991 --> 33:16.786
We'll give you a short overview
of the changes first,

33:16.869 --> 33:18.496
then we will take questions, okay?

33:24.836 --> 33:28.172
Our data now shows the drop
in temperature is remaining strong

33:28.256 --> 33:30.383
throughout the next three or four days.

33:30.466 --> 33:32.135
The cold wave, which the forecast

33:32.218 --> 33:34.345
previously had subsiding
tomorrow afternoon

33:34.429 --> 33:37.306
is now expected to last until this weekend

33:37.390 --> 33:40.226
around Korea's center
and the southern inland regions.

33:40.309 --> 33:41.602
- Okay. Bye.
- Okay.

33:41.686 --> 33:42.854
- Okay.
- Bye.

33:44.313 --> 33:46.274
- Okay. Bye.
- Bye.

34:00.872 --> 34:01.789
Aren't you going home?

34:02.290 --> 34:04.083
You go on. I'm gonna review this.

34:52.090 --> 34:53.216
Thank you.

34:56.552 --> 34:58.513
The jet stream will stay, right?

34:58.596 --> 35:02.350
Only the jet stream knows
what the jet stream's gonna do.

35:02.433 --> 35:04.268
The forecast is already out.

35:04.352 --> 35:06.062
So stop going over and go home.

35:06.646 --> 35:09.357
I'll stay and hold down
the fort here, huh?

35:16.155 --> 35:19.367
- Oh, hey, earlier--
- I'm sorry about before.

35:21.244 --> 35:23.579
You were just asking
'cause you care about him,

35:23.663 --> 35:25.039
and I got defensive.

35:28.751 --> 35:30.294
You're right about me too.

35:30.378 --> 35:33.714
I keep acting like a child
when we talk about him.

35:34.298 --> 35:37.677
I try to stay rational, but it's so hard.

35:38.886 --> 35:40.763
It's always been like that.

35:41.347 --> 35:43.057
My relationships start well.

35:44.559 --> 35:45.768
But my father…

35:46.978 --> 35:48.646
always ruins it.

35:51.399 --> 35:53.568
I just find him so tiring.

35:53.651 --> 35:58.364
It's my own father, and…
I didn't want to make the woman I love

35:58.447 --> 36:01.450
have to deal with him
as part of the family.

36:04.829 --> 36:06.080
Can't love be enough?

36:07.623 --> 36:10.209
Not everyone has to become family.

36:11.419 --> 36:15.840
The world keeps telling you
to take responsibility for your love,

36:16.883 --> 36:19.177
and that marriage is the only way
to do that.

36:19.802 --> 36:20.803
So…

36:23.222 --> 36:24.724
I told her we're over.

36:49.582 --> 36:50.666
I'm sorry.

36:56.214 --> 36:59.133
It's okay. You don't have to apologize.

36:59.926 --> 37:00.927
I get it.

37:05.348 --> 37:08.601
Really, I… I understand.

37:16.317 --> 37:17.193
Lee Si-woo.

37:19.237 --> 37:20.821
Why do you keep saying it's fine?

37:22.240 --> 37:25.910
Why do you keep telling me
that you understand why?

37:30.414 --> 37:33.501
What are you gonna do
if I try to get you back?

37:36.587 --> 37:38.130
If I beg and beg you,

37:39.048 --> 37:40.925
tell you that I just can't lose you…

37:51.519 --> 37:52.895
I still…

37:54.981 --> 37:56.857
like you a lot, Director.

37:59.944 --> 38:01.070
You know that?

38:09.662 --> 38:12.039
Hey! Where is Director Jin?

38:12.623 --> 38:14.709
Director Jin! Hey!

38:20.047 --> 38:21.465
Hey, yo, Director!

38:22.091 --> 38:24.176
Director Jin Ha-kyung!

38:24.260 --> 38:25.261
Let's talk later.

38:29.598 --> 38:31.475
Where's Director Jin?

38:32.268 --> 38:34.437
She screws up the entire forecast
and goes home already?

38:34.520 --> 38:36.397
Somebody go call your director!

38:37.440 --> 38:38.357
I'm here.

38:38.858 --> 38:43.321
You, who… Who said you
could redact a forecast, huh?

38:44.196 --> 38:46.449
The jet stream at 10 kilometers
is still strong.

38:47.033 --> 38:48.701
We don't believe it will clear.

38:48.784 --> 38:49.702
Hey.

38:50.453 --> 38:53.873
You think that Team One just adapts
your forecast like we're stupid?

38:53.956 --> 38:56.667
No, it's because we respect
the work the other team did.

38:56.751 --> 38:58.836
And we understand
the prior team's analysis

38:58.919 --> 39:01.088
is the most reliable source material.

39:01.172 --> 39:03.257
How dare you go and just throw
all our hard work away?

39:03.341 --> 39:05.843
It's not that I don't value
all your efforts.

39:05.926 --> 39:07.595
We revise predictions due to new evidence.

39:07.678 --> 39:09.722
And? What if you made a mistake?

39:09.805 --> 39:11.766
Who's gonna be responsible for this?

39:11.849 --> 39:14.018
Are you gonna take the fall
for the human lives at stake

39:14.101 --> 39:15.144
and the billions in costs?

39:15.227 --> 39:18.356
Are you saying when there's
an irregular pattern, I should do nothing

39:18.439 --> 39:21.317
just because someone more senior to me
is emotionally attached to their forecast?

39:21.400 --> 39:22.443
Huh?

39:29.075 --> 39:31.327
HEADQUARTERS
SHIN SEOK-HO

39:31.410 --> 39:32.870
Hmm, Mr. Shin here.

39:33.537 --> 39:35.414
Sir, where are you right now?
Are you near?

39:36.207 --> 39:39.293
Uh, I think you'll have
to come in again tonight.

39:39.377 --> 39:41.545
Why? What's going on?

39:41.629 --> 39:42.963
Director Choi from Chief Team One

39:43.047 --> 39:45.466
is raising hell here
about the redaction earlier.

39:45.549 --> 39:48.969
What did you just say?

39:49.053 --> 39:50.304
Say that one more time!

39:51.222 --> 39:53.933
- Say that one more time!
- Oh, no!

39:54.016 --> 39:56.560
- What do you think a director is, huh?
- Hey! Hey! Hey!

39:56.644 --> 39:58.896
- Director.
- Hey! What's going on?

39:58.979 --> 40:01.399
I gotta see my daughter now!

40:01.482 --> 40:04.985
It's her birthday! We're supposed
to eat out tonight! Come on!

40:05.069 --> 40:07.071
- …say to me?
- What are you doing, huh?

40:07.154 --> 40:09.448
- Who are you?
- We're talking.

40:09.532 --> 40:12.159
All that praise got to your head,
and now you're lost, huh?

40:12.243 --> 40:14.829
Apologize for what you just said
to me right now!

40:14.912 --> 40:16.038
Just say sorry!

40:18.707 --> 40:22.169
I won't. Everything I said
is exactly what I mean.

40:23.754 --> 40:25.965
Whoa!

40:26.048 --> 40:28.759
You turned into a real brat now, huh?

40:28.843 --> 40:30.553
- Stop--
- Who the hell are you?

40:30.636 --> 40:34.140
I'll show you how we handle
behavior like this around here.

40:34.223 --> 40:35.307
Now, what did you say to me?

40:35.391 --> 40:36.892
- Go on! Say it again, huh?
- Let go!

40:36.976 --> 40:39.019
- Let go!
- Say it again!

40:39.103 --> 40:40.271
I said let go of her!

41:00.833 --> 41:02.293
SENIOR FORECASTER UM DONG-HAN

41:02.376 --> 41:03.419
Hello?

41:05.045 --> 41:06.213
What was that?

41:07.131 --> 41:08.174
Seok-ho.

41:10.468 --> 41:11.385
Seok-ho?

41:17.516 --> 41:19.435
Si-woo.

41:27.526 --> 41:30.070
Oh, my goodness!
I can't believe it finally happened.

41:34.575 --> 41:37.244
Yes, sir. This is Assistant Director Park.

41:37.328 --> 41:38.162
What?

41:46.879 --> 41:49.673
For crying…

42:01.685 --> 42:04.188
I can't believe Appa
got a reservation here.

42:05.689 --> 42:07.775
You said you wanted to go somewhere nice.

42:08.442 --> 42:10.653
- This place is really trendy, Ma.
- Hmm.

42:10.736 --> 42:14.156
I was looking it up,
and tons of famous people come here.

42:14.240 --> 42:17.368
It's the hottest place
in Cheongdam-dong these days.

42:17.451 --> 42:19.161
I heard it's really hard to get into.

42:19.245 --> 42:22.414
Really? That's not like your Appa.

42:22.498 --> 42:24.333
I guess he really made an effort.

42:27.044 --> 42:29.046
Uh, what should we get?

42:36.220 --> 42:37.805
BO-MI'S DAD

42:49.358 --> 42:51.110
Yes. What? Where are you right now?

42:51.694 --> 42:52.570
I…

42:53.195 --> 42:54.613
I was headed there.

42:55.197 --> 42:57.074
And, well… And I…

42:57.157 --> 42:59.910
I just got a call
from the office. There's this…

42:59.994 --> 43:00.869
Forget it.

43:00.953 --> 43:02.204
Hyang-rae, I…

43:02.288 --> 43:03.831
- I'll be there--
- I said fine.

43:12.214 --> 43:14.383
What? Appa's not coming?

43:17.970 --> 43:20.389
Yeah. You're dad had to…

43:22.099 --> 43:23.684
Today, of all days, hmm…

43:24.893 --> 43:27.438
- What should we do?
- Let's just eat by ourselves.

43:31.567 --> 43:33.527
Can I order the two things I want?

43:33.611 --> 43:35.362
I don't know when I'll come here again.

43:45.789 --> 43:48.250
This is just
a habit to you, huh?

43:49.460 --> 43:51.420
It was just an accident, Director.

43:51.503 --> 43:54.590
He was trying to stop the fight.
It was an accident.

43:55.466 --> 43:57.593
You were the one who started it, Director.

43:57.676 --> 44:01.305
Forecaster Si-woo here
was trying to break it up, that's all.

44:01.805 --> 44:04.558
Oh, right. Break it up, huh?

44:04.642 --> 44:07.853
Forecaster, this isn't your first time
assaulting someone, is it?

44:08.520 --> 44:11.774
I heard you punched
Han Ki-jun at the Spokesman's Office.

44:11.857 --> 44:13.859
If you wanna vent, take it out on me.

44:13.942 --> 44:16.028
Don't go harassing all of Team Two.

44:16.111 --> 44:17.446
Hey, Jin Ha-kyung.

44:17.529 --> 44:19.948
You should worry about the forecast,
not all these guys.

44:20.032 --> 44:22.493
What will you do when your forecast
is wrong after your redaction?

44:23.077 --> 44:25.871
What would you want, huh?
For me to resign?

44:26.789 --> 44:28.123
You just said it. You'll resign.

44:28.207 --> 44:30.000
Director, please just calm down.

44:30.084 --> 44:31.794
But if our forecast is correct,

44:31.877 --> 44:34.171
well, then, you should be
the one to resign, Director.

44:34.254 --> 44:36.340
- What?
- What is this, huh, Squid Game?

44:36.423 --> 44:37.925
One of you dies if you lose?

44:38.008 --> 44:40.803
Team One versus Team Two,
Director, and the loser resigns.

44:40.886 --> 44:44.264
We'll go down in KMA history books,
as an example of reckless leadership, huh?

44:44.348 --> 44:45.432
How about it? Let's go.

44:45.516 --> 44:47.101
You snarky little…

44:47.184 --> 44:48.519
Stop it! Stop!

44:48.602 --> 44:51.105
Give it a rest, people, huh?

44:51.188 --> 44:54.066
What are you fighting about?
Is your nose bleeding?

44:57.486 --> 44:58.696
What are you doing?

44:59.279 --> 45:03.158
Why? What are you people doing here
just fighting over weather?

45:04.326 --> 45:05.411
I didn't hit anyone.

45:05.994 --> 45:07.955
Uh, I… hit him.

45:08.539 --> 45:09.832
It was an accident.

45:09.915 --> 45:11.792
No, really, it was.

45:12.501 --> 45:14.670
They came at me three to one.

45:15.295 --> 45:18.757
I wanna make this clear.
I was trying to stop the fight.

45:20.092 --> 45:22.678
Never mind that.
Senior Forecaster Um.

45:22.761 --> 45:24.847
How do you train all these guys?
They're a mess!

45:24.930 --> 45:26.473
I told you that weather is a fluid thing,

45:26.557 --> 45:29.476
not something you can reverse
with a few numbers. I told you that!

45:29.560 --> 45:32.604
And then, you all have
to run and go throw away

45:32.688 --> 45:36.275
weeks of analysis just because
there's a couple ensemble scenarios

45:36.358 --> 45:37.609
that look odd?

45:37.693 --> 45:39.027
What?

45:39.111 --> 45:41.780
You redacted my forecast before too.

45:42.281 --> 45:44.158
- I did?
- You did?

45:44.241 --> 45:45.200
Two times, yeah.

45:46.452 --> 45:47.786
Really? Twice?

45:48.996 --> 45:50.205
And when did I do that?

45:50.289 --> 45:54.418
2004, summer heat wave.
2011 fall, the cold air.

45:54.501 --> 45:56.086
You got one right, and I got one right.

45:56.170 --> 45:57.796
But I… I never scolded you

45:57.880 --> 46:00.090
about the times that you went
and messed with it.

46:00.174 --> 46:01.508
Because I…

46:01.592 --> 46:05.220
I had faith in you, absolute!
And I thought you were sure.

46:05.304 --> 46:09.266
But you're… you're a senior!
You should have the same faith in her! No?

46:09.850 --> 46:13.187
Instead you come here
and make a mess 'cause of one revision?

46:13.270 --> 46:17.483
'Cause she's a little snot.
We can't talk if she won't listen to us!

46:17.566 --> 46:18.609
Director Choi.

46:19.526 --> 46:21.195
She's Team Two's director.

46:22.529 --> 46:24.239
She's the same rank as you.

46:24.323 --> 46:27.785
Director Jin has the same responsibility
and authority as you.

46:28.786 --> 46:31.413
How are you gonna come in here
and push her around with age?

46:31.497 --> 46:34.041
It's not the '80s, man! "Snot"?

46:34.124 --> 46:35.542
Is our director a child?

46:40.672 --> 46:42.841
So I got a little angry, huh? So what?

46:42.925 --> 46:45.260
Yeah, you got that angry
over a weather issue.

46:45.344 --> 46:47.888
Trust me, no one's as angry
as I am here, okay?

46:47.971 --> 46:50.057
It's my daughter's birthday dinner now!

46:50.140 --> 46:52.684
I was going to have
a normal meal out with her

46:52.768 --> 46:55.187
for the first real time in ten years.

46:55.270 --> 46:56.605
I even did my hair.

46:56.688 --> 47:00.859
I was gonna be a real dad for once,
and now they're probably already done!

47:08.450 --> 47:11.119
Excuse me. The difference
in atmospheric pressure

47:11.203 --> 47:12.955
around Siberia is dropping.

47:15.374 --> 47:18.210
What the…

47:18.836 --> 47:19.670
Ms. Lee.

47:19.753 --> 47:23.131
Track back the hourly development
situation in the global model.

47:23.715 --> 47:24.633
Hmm.

47:28.804 --> 47:30.472
The jet stream is moving south.

47:31.223 --> 47:32.307
The… the…

47:33.141 --> 47:36.103
The… Well, it shouldn't be falling.

47:41.316 --> 47:42.734
Go home. Your shift's over.

47:44.778 --> 47:45.612
Go home.

47:49.992 --> 47:51.159
Damn it!

48:18.395 --> 48:20.606
Door is opening.

48:22.357 --> 48:23.734
- Hello.
- Hello.

48:30.782 --> 48:32.117
Door is closing.

48:40.751 --> 48:41.835
Oppa.

48:44.129 --> 48:46.506
It's late. You're still working?

48:47.299 --> 48:48.216
Mm.

48:48.717 --> 48:50.886
I'm just not feeling too great.

48:57.017 --> 48:59.728
I was worried. You looked white
as a sheet in the press room.

49:01.772 --> 49:03.231
Does it hurt anywhere else?

49:03.899 --> 49:05.567
Mm, no, I'm okay.

49:08.654 --> 49:11.907
I've been thinking, Yu-jin.

49:13.784 --> 49:15.035
The kid…

49:17.245 --> 49:18.163
I'm grateful for it.

49:24.252 --> 49:25.420
I know…

49:26.505 --> 49:28.215
I'm not ready as a father right now.

49:30.467 --> 49:33.887
And when it comes,
there'll be moments when I flounder

49:34.471 --> 49:35.889
and lose my cool.

49:35.973 --> 49:38.684
And I know I'll look like
such a fool when it happens.

49:40.227 --> 49:41.937
It's our kid, though.

49:43.146 --> 49:44.856
And I wanna do my very best.

49:47.651 --> 49:49.903
- Oppa, I--
- But…

49:50.570 --> 49:53.490
even if I feel that way,
if you're not sure, Yu-jin,

49:55.158 --> 49:56.410
I'll honor your choices.

49:58.912 --> 50:01.415
I don't wanna force that sacrifice on you.

50:06.294 --> 50:12.884
All I can tell you now is that really,
no matter what you decide,

50:14.136 --> 50:15.595
I will be there for you.

50:16.680 --> 50:20.183
I'm gonna be right there the whole time,

50:21.977 --> 50:23.145
so you won't be alone.

50:33.196 --> 50:34.948
I'm hungry.

50:35.574 --> 50:36.533
Wanna go eat?

51:53.401 --> 51:54.986
Whoa! All this?

51:55.779 --> 51:59.199
I have the ingredients
so I thought I would, you know.

51:59.282 --> 52:00.742
Well, it smells great.

52:01.326 --> 52:03.328
My mom and I are both great cooks.

52:03.912 --> 52:04.788
Wow!

52:15.257 --> 52:16.133
Whoa!

52:16.800 --> 52:17.968
Is there anything that…

52:18.718 --> 52:20.762
that you're not great at, huh?

52:21.513 --> 52:24.057
You're a great artist,
great cook, great charisma.

52:24.141 --> 52:26.184
You think?

52:28.478 --> 52:30.689
You're great at, well, everything
except writing stories.

52:38.405 --> 52:40.073
What about my stories?

52:40.157 --> 52:42.117
What don't you like about them?

52:42.200 --> 52:45.036
Mm-mm. No, it's just that…

52:45.620 --> 52:46.705
They're not bad.

52:46.788 --> 52:50.375
They don't have a hook,
something that hooks you in.

52:51.751 --> 52:55.130
Oh, a hook, okay.

52:55.213 --> 52:59.509
Yeah. But your artwork's
still super cute, right?

53:01.386 --> 53:02.679
Mmm…

53:08.351 --> 53:10.228
So what you're saying
is my stories are bad

53:10.312 --> 53:12.397
because they don't have a hook, right?

53:13.190 --> 53:17.277
No. Uh, well, I never said bad, really.

53:17.360 --> 53:19.279
And that my writing doesn't sell.

53:19.863 --> 53:21.364
I don't think I said that.

53:21.448 --> 53:25.410
You were suggesting it when you said
that the hooks in my stories were lacking.

53:31.666 --> 53:34.377
Well… wine? Want it?

53:34.461 --> 53:37.088
- Here. You want some, hmm?
- No.

53:38.381 --> 53:39.799
I wanna talk about my writing.

53:47.891 --> 53:50.060
Door is opening.

53:53.897 --> 53:55.523
Door is closing.

54:03.406 --> 54:04.241
Huh?

54:14.709 --> 54:17.254
Did she change the password
for her front door?

54:29.516 --> 54:31.309
Did you change your password?

54:31.893 --> 54:35.188
Yes, recently. I deserve my privacy.

54:35.272 --> 54:38.233
Enough of that!
Now what is the new combination?

54:39.359 --> 54:41.236
I'm sorry, Mom. I'll see you later.

54:46.658 --> 54:48.034
You could have told her.

54:48.535 --> 54:49.661
It's cold out.

54:50.996 --> 54:53.248
It's okay. She's stronger than you think.

55:01.214 --> 55:04.426
So where are we going right now?

55:07.220 --> 55:08.096
The doctor.

55:10.557 --> 55:12.392
Heartless little wench.

55:13.601 --> 55:16.604
How can this girl of mine
be so cold-hearted?

55:19.399 --> 55:23.028
What should I do?
I can't just take all of these back now.

55:32.912 --> 55:33.955
Tell me!

55:34.039 --> 55:37.459
Tell me what you don't like
about my stories and be specific.

55:38.209 --> 55:41.629
It's… not that I don't like them. It's…

55:42.589 --> 55:44.716
Why do you keep saying
opposite things, huh?

55:44.799 --> 55:48.470
I'm serious! You said there
wasn't a hook, so explain, huh?

55:48.553 --> 55:50.513
Oh, the hook. It's, um…

55:51.514 --> 55:54.768
You're a lot more, uh, persistent
than I thought you would be.

55:55.518 --> 55:58.813
You can't be a writer if you're not
a persistent person, you know.

55:58.897 --> 56:01.775
For all those hours and days
you draw, and write and rewrite,

56:01.858 --> 56:03.860
and edit, and slave over your art.

56:03.943 --> 56:06.946
Have you ever laid awake all night
because you couldn't think

56:07.030 --> 56:08.990
of this one word you were looking for?

56:09.783 --> 56:11.951
I spend a week agonizing over one line,

56:12.035 --> 56:14.079
until my head feels
like it's gonna explode!

56:14.162 --> 56:17.207
I keep writing and rewriting
for what feels like forever!

56:17.290 --> 56:21.252
Every noun, every last article,
I write and rewrite 10,000 times,

56:21.336 --> 56:23.797
hoping I can make
even one sentence more dynamic,

56:23.880 --> 56:28.009
hoping I can better express myself
and just hoping it will work for someone.

56:28.843 --> 56:29.928
I'm sorry.

56:30.512 --> 56:32.889
And I know you can just look
at the final product,

56:32.972 --> 56:34.974
and say, "Oh, it's bad or it needs work."

56:35.058 --> 56:37.644
But don't be so quick to judge
my work and just ignore

56:37.727 --> 56:39.354
all the effort that it takes.

56:40.522 --> 56:42.315
I never did that.

56:43.274 --> 56:47.570
I'm an unpopular author
who can't sell a copy.

56:47.654 --> 56:49.447
But I have my pride still.

56:50.115 --> 56:53.326
I pride myself in knowing
that at least my writing

56:53.868 --> 56:56.955
and illustrations are gonna help
some children

56:57.038 --> 56:59.833
have a little more sunshine
in their lives, okay?

57:00.875 --> 57:02.752
Of course. I'll keep that in mind.

57:03.461 --> 57:04.879
All right, then.

57:07.382 --> 57:09.426
Don't go.

57:12.011 --> 57:13.054
Tae-kyung.

57:14.389 --> 57:15.390
Tae-kyung.

57:17.100 --> 57:18.351
You can't just go.

57:19.102 --> 57:20.812
What do you want me to do?

57:23.523 --> 57:24.816
I'm really…

57:26.359 --> 57:27.861
really sorry about it.

57:29.362 --> 57:30.488
Don't leave, okay?

57:51.384 --> 57:53.511
Oh, dear. Oh, dear. What do I do?

58:01.769 --> 58:03.605
- Ooh!
- Whoa!

58:04.814 --> 58:06.691
Are you okay?

58:06.774 --> 58:08.693
- Are you good? Are you good?
- Oh, my god.

58:08.776 --> 58:10.278
- Are you all right?
- Oh, dear!

58:18.453 --> 58:19.496
Tae… Tae-kyung.

58:20.079 --> 58:21.080
Yes?

58:28.171 --> 58:31.674
Oh! Uh… Uh…

58:32.300 --> 58:35.053
- What? What?
- Huh?

58:36.262 --> 58:37.472
You!

58:38.056 --> 58:40.058
Jin Tae-kyung!

58:40.141 --> 58:42.936
- Mom! Mom!
- Please calm down, ma'am!

58:43.019 --> 58:45.688
CHAYOUNG HOSPITAL

58:52.737 --> 58:53.947
Is somebody sick?

58:55.198 --> 58:56.324
Room 309.

58:57.450 --> 58:59.577
The attending physician's on call today.

59:01.287 --> 59:02.914
So you can go in and…

59:39.784 --> 59:42.412
LEE MYUNG-HAN

01:00:20.825 --> 01:00:24.120
We have the PET CT results
and the sputum results as well.

01:00:25.622 --> 01:00:27.957
And, well, it's… it's cancer.

01:00:28.041 --> 01:00:30.585
It's already advanced to stage three.

01:00:32.003 --> 01:00:36.215
If you take a look
at the PET CT scan here,

01:00:37.467 --> 01:00:40.637
it's metastasized
above the lymph nodes on the right.

01:00:44.932 --> 01:00:47.435
He must have been
in a great deal of pain.

01:01:06.996 --> 01:01:08.081
Appa.

01:01:24.305 --> 01:01:26.182
Why would you do this to me?

01:01:28.267 --> 01:01:29.310
Why?

01:01:32.438 --> 01:01:33.481
Why?

01:01:35.274 --> 01:01:37.026
Why are you doing this?

01:02:10.309 --> 01:02:11.269
Excuse me.

01:02:12.186 --> 01:02:14.272
Is a Mr. Lee Myung-han here?

01:02:14.856 --> 01:02:16.691
They brought him in for a car crash.

01:02:16.774 --> 01:02:17.900
What do you need?

01:02:28.953 --> 01:02:30.830
- Oppa.
- Hmm?

01:02:32.039 --> 01:02:34.250
- Help me.
- What is it?

01:02:36.335 --> 01:02:38.838
- My stomach.
- Huh?

01:02:42.049 --> 01:02:43.718
Yu-jin, what's… what's wrong?
Where does it hurt?

01:02:43.801 --> 01:02:45.553
My stomach hurts so much.

01:02:46.137 --> 01:02:48.514
Hey, Yu-jin, what's wrong, huh?
Hey, Yu-jin, huh?

01:02:53.102 --> 01:02:55.855
The rain said to the wind…

01:02:59.400 --> 01:03:01.027
What's your relationship
with Lee Myung-han?

01:03:03.112 --> 01:03:04.405
Well, his guardian.

01:03:05.782 --> 01:03:06.991
We're the police.

01:03:07.742 --> 01:03:10.286
There's an arrest warrant out
for Mr. Lee Myung-han.

01:03:10.369 --> 01:03:12.872
Charges are extortion and insurance fraud.

01:03:37.688 --> 01:03:38.940
"You roar."

01:03:41.776 --> 01:03:43.402
"And I'll fall."

01:04:12.348 --> 01:04:15.101
I found out
that getting something wrong

01:04:15.184 --> 01:04:17.645
can often teach you
more than getting something right.

01:04:17.728 --> 01:04:19.730
Do you know what the most
ridiculous thing in the world

01:04:19.814 --> 01:04:20.940
you can say is?

01:04:21.524 --> 01:04:23.401
That you're breaking up out of love.

01:04:24.652 --> 01:04:25.945
Don't let Lee Si-woo go.

01:04:26.028 --> 01:04:28.614
Not for Lee Si-woo, but for yourself.

01:04:30.074 --> 01:04:32.243
Because it's you, Jin Ha-kyung.

01:04:34.161 --> 01:04:36.956
Because it's you, Lee Si-woo.

01:04:39.208 --> 01:04:41.460
Because I just like you.

01:04:42.587 --> 01:04:44.297
Because I like being with you.
